WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.520
Is there a lasting goal that keeps me motivated—one that never gets outdated or loses its effect, and has no harmful side effects?

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:20.160
This is an option to consider. We have to admit one fact.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.800
What fact? Everything we just put on the left…

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:33.720
It is human nature—something we cannot escape or shake off.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:43.280
Some religions teach self-salvation: train yourself and try to change human nature by your own effort.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:54.400
It is like an elite weightlifter trying to lift himself.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.680
Can he do it?

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:05.320
He can lift more than his own weight and many other things, but there is one thing he cannot lift: himself.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:10.800
That is why we say, “You can’t pull yourself out.”

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.560
If I am stuck in a swamp, I cannot pull myself out. How could someone else stuck there pull me out?

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.080
The harder he pulls, the deeper he sinks.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:25.560
So we are all in the swamp, with the human nature shown on the left.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.920
We cannot save ourselves, and we cannot save others either.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:39.160
People cannot pull themselves out. I may be able to help others, but I cannot pull myself out.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:49.920
There are countless examples. Many people know video games waste their youth. Why do they keep playing?

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.480
They cannot break free.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:02:04.200
We know many things are wrong; we know they feel empty and meaningless. Why do we keep doing them?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.800
We cannot break free. Another reason may be that there seems to be no better option.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:16.320
So today we want to offer a better option.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.600
The better option is on the right.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:29.720
This is what we all long for. This is the divine nature.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:43.920
Only God has these qualities: lasting, unchanging, incorruptible, enduring, forever pure, unshakable, completely reliable, all-powerful, and eternal.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.260
This is not human. This is God.
